From 013c0c7f93206e819d5c1791c3f8d6112b38a259 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?R=C3=A9mi=20Fabre?= <remi.fabre@pollen-robotics.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:43:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/29] robot.rebootMotors: reboot servos in place, `robotctl
 robot reboot-motors`, D-pad-up on the pad

A servo that trips its shutdown mask (overload, overheating, electrical shock) latches with
torque off until it is rebooted or the battery is pulled. This adds the REBOOT instruction as
an IO primitive and one intent on top of it:

- `duck_control::io::RobotIo::reboot(id)` (rustypot's reboot; FakeIo records it) and
  `Safety::reboot_motors(ids)`, which also forgets the gain cache: a rebooted XL330 comes
  back at its EEPROM gains, and a cache that still says "200 is written" would leave it there.
- `robot.rebootMotors { ids }`: torque off on every joint, REBOOT the ids named (all of them
  when the list is empty), back to limp. `init` / Start brings the robot up again. Refused
  over Bluetooth like `relax`; allowed on the console like `relax`.
- `robotctl robot reboot-motors [ID ...]`: no ids = every servo, ids space separated (#201
  asked for commas; spaces are what a shell hands over naturally).
- padd: a short D-pad-up press and release reboots every servo. The 3 s hold still switches
  walk/roller and does not reboot.

Closes #201.
