From db2c70efe43c0562aec1fd2f614b0df706169aad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?R=C3=A9mi=20Fabre?= <remi.fabre@pollen-robotics.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 16:16:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/29] padd: Start once stands the robot up (robot.init),
 Start again drives

The first Start on a booted duck used to run the gait straight out of the home ramp. The pad
now keeps a belief of whether the robot is up: false at start and after the soften / recover /
shutdown it sent, true after its init. Not up: Start sends robot.init (torque on, 2 s ramp,
hold). Up: Start toggles the policy as before.
---
 docs/robot/cheatsheet.md |  2 +-
 padd/src/main.rs         | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

